      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The pathway to citizenship and expanded humanitarian processing framework is far superior for long-term stability because it directly addresses the root causes of migration by offering dignity and economic opportunity to vulnerable populations. Relying solely on increased border enforcement and surveillance tech creates a temporary, punitive fix that fails to solve the underlying demographic and economic pressures driving migration. A humane approach fosters social cohesion and a more skilled workforce, whereas aggressive enforcement often fuels resentment and instability without delivering sustainable economic growth.",
      "source": "target",
